@toggle more_detail = false (label: "Show additional context")

## First, open your file

@when platform == "macOS"
Open the local HTML file in a browser from Finder.

- Keep the source `.tinta` separately for editing.
- A `.tinta.zip` keeps local images with the source.
@end

@when platform == "Windows"
Open the local HTML file in a browser from File Explorer.

The reader does not require an account or a local application server.
@end

@when platform == "Linux"
Open the local HTML file using your browser's **Open file** action.

```text
This code block is descriptive only. Nothing here executes.
```
@end

@when more_detail
### What is inside the file?

An interactive export contains all source data and hidden explanations.
A static export contains the resolved visible document instead.

@details "Why the distinction matters"
Hiding an explanation in an interactive file does not make it confidential.
@end
@end

